      "writtenOn": "2023-11-06T15:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. I had asked Takuto this earlier and he said it was meant to be run directly by users: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/767956/comments/c4e073f7_6e15aff8\n\nSo I was reviewing it with that guidance in mind, but I can readjust my expectations accordingly :)\n\nAs a guide, this is a useful resource, and hopefully we can take the migration from here and write up a doc similar to go/goma-skia. We still have questions about Windows, but we\u0027ll cross that bridge when we come to it. \n\nI also would like a little clarity on versioning. This script hardcodes `re_client_version:0.116.1.9128bc4-gomaip` but presumably the version changes regularly. How can we keep current with the latest version? Can the updating be automatic/invisible to users? With goma we did not need to think about version updates.",
      "parentUuid": "3dc79994_af208a77",
      "revId": "bf6cdf402d63d0d8790f621c9851f6758af94838",
